on march 18th hogwarts legacy community  manager chandler wood answered the  following question on twitter where is  the angry tree aka whomping willow is  the secret passage to honeydukes going  to be included you should keep in mind  the official website shows what appears  to be a whopping willow-like tree here  and it also appears in an official  wallpaper released for the game and this  makes chandler's response even more  interesting because he said the whomping  willow wasn't planted until 1971. our  game takes place about 80 years before  that i can't confirm or deny specific  secret passages but i can say that the  world is filled with secrets mysteries  and nods to plenty of wizarding world  lore okay we definitely have to talk  about that second part on secret  passages but regarding the whomping  willow of course potter fans will know  that wood is absolutely correct here  with his timing on the whopping willow  we know from the original series in  harry potter and the prisoner of azkaban  remus lupin tells harry i told you  months ago that the whomping willow was  planted the year i came to hogwarts the  truth is that it was planted because i  came to hogwarts so what does wood's  response and what we know about the  whomping willow mean for the tree still  pictured on the hogwarts legacy website  i see only two possibilities here the  first is the tree we see pictured here  isn't actually a whomping willow at all  and honestly this is entirely possible  danny allen is a dev who worked on the  game and he actually responded to a  twitter question all the way back in  june of 2021 saying here we know better  than to use that but even though this is  completely possible i actually don't  think it's probable i do expect us to  come across a whomping willow in the  game first let's take a closer look at  some of the artwork avalanche shared in  the developer behind the scenes  interview and you'll find even more  trees that look similar to a whomping  willow i'm not saying they're all for  sure a whomping willow type tree but  some of them definitely look pretty  close you see while as harry potter fans  we often think of it as the whomping  willow because of its significance in  the original series it's actually just a  normal magical plant at least normal for  the wizarding world that is which means  there could be plenty of other whomping  willows out there in fact some of them  could even be very near hogwarts and  even in parts of the forbidden forest  we've never seen before avalanche talks  a lot about venturing beyond the walls  of hogwarts and exploring the  surrounding countryside so personally i  still expect we'll come across one or  two throughout the game it just won't be  the exact whomping willow we remember  from the days of lupin so i still  believe the tree we see pictured on the  website and some of the trees in this  artwork could be a whopping willow that  we'll see in the game i think a tree  that physically attacks and defends its  territory just lends itself so well to a  video game there are all sorts of  gameplay scenarios they could frame  around this whether it's a magical  creature who is maybe trapped near one  and needs rescuing or even one that's  protecting some sort of magical artifact  or who knows in a nod to the original  series maybe even something protecting a  secret passage i mentioned we also need  to talk about wood's response regarding  secret passages and this is absolutely  music to the ears of long time fans i  mean he didn't outright confirm secret  passages but he kind of did right  hogwarts contained so many secrets we  know even dumbledore admitted that he  didn't know all of them and considering  the school was made by two incredibly  powerful witches and two ridiculously  powerful wizards it all makes sense they  likely even kept many secrets from one  another about the castle and honestly  this is an area where avalanche can  really let their creativity shine  through because of how much freedom  there is to do something new and then  balance that with the familiar locations  that we all already know and love within  hogwarts when it comes specifically to  secret passages there are a few we know  about already that have a chance to be  in the game there's the one-eyed witch  statue which led to honeydukes a statue  of gregory the smarmy that leads  somewhere outside of hogwarts a mirror  on the fourth floor that led to  hogsmeade plus three others that fred  and george say they don't use because  filch already knows about them of course  this is all many years later in harry  potter's day the borgin and burke's  vanishing cabinets are another  possibility as they could have been  functional in this time period but we  don't know the exact date of their  creation and then there's also the  secret passage that was guarded by the  whomping willow that led to the  shrieking shack but of course neither  the whomping willow nor the shrieking  shack will be there in 1890. so this  question on the whomping willow is  actually just one of many questions i  still have about hogwarts legacy in fact  there are seven big questions we still  don't know the answer to and i have a  full video exploring those which you can  see on the right side of your screen now  as always thank you all so much for  watching i'll talk to you again soon
 

